positions.description:
CREA launched the sous-vide revolution when it opened its doors in Paris more than two decades ago. Since then, we’ve trained many of the world’s most celebrated chefs. We’re changing the way the world cooks and the definition of fine dining.

Marketing
• Work as a liaison among international teams: U.S, France, UAE and Thailand;
• Oversee 11 social media accounts to include creating content, managing paid and
influencer campaigns and interacting with followers;
• Determine marketing plans, strategies and monitor budget to cater to marketing
needs of 10 different sales channels, both B2B and B2C;
• Work with outside vendors (agencies, printers, event planners, photographers,
videographers, etc.) on projects and campaigns;
• Assist in marketing outreach, market analysis and distribution activities;
• Manage a database of 10,000+ contacts for email campaigns and newsletters;
• Prepare creative and visually pleasing marketing materials, brochures, presentation
decks and training booklets;
• Write, edit, review, proofread content for Sous-Vide Magazine;
• Assist with the production of all print, web and electronic materials from conception
to completion;
• Lead photoshoots and video shoots. Experienced with both pre- and postproduction
processes: developing storyboard, script, layout, art direction,
photographing, filming and editing;
• Train and onboard new team members.

Sales
• Successfully lead paid campaigns and ads breaking the sales record of
Sous-Vide Trainings;
• Nurture potential customers for conversion and current customers for retention;
• Handle training registrations, create quotes and invoices for sales;
• Manage online store and troubleshoot any technical and logistic issues;
• Manage store inventory and fulfill equipment sales.

Events
• Organize training events and seminars domestically and internationally;
• Assist the event team in planning and provide digital coverage;
• Provide V/A support at events and seminars.

