The Association for Unmanned Vehicle Systems International (AUVSI) — the world's largest nonprofit organization dedicated to the advancement of unmanned systems and robotics — represents more than 7,500 members from more than 60 countries involved in the fields of government, industry and academia. AUVSI members work in the defense, civil and commercial markets.

• Work under the Marketing Department on the AUVSI XPONENTIAL 2018 and Automated Vehicles Symposium 2018.

Some responsibilities include:
• Website:
1. Manage AUVSI's main website (www.auvsi.org) as well as event websites (www.xponential.org; www.automatedvehiclessymposium.org; www.thedefenseshow.org; www.faa.auvsi.net);
2. Build and maintain over 60 public facing web pages on three different platforms – Higher Logic, Drupal & A2Z;
3. Handle and process day-of requests (~15 a day)
5. Create hero images for new web pages.
4. Optimize web pages for maximum user experience.

• Social Media:
1. Create over 100 customized images to accompany social media posts on Facebook, Twitter, Instagram and LinkedIn;
2. Create Snapchat filters for XPONENTIAL 2018.

• Barters:
1. Create over 50 customized design suites (emails, digital ads and print ads) for partner organizations using Photoshop, Illustrator and InDesign;
2. Ensure consistency across signage, web pages and print pieces.
3. Conduct research projects upon request.

• Email:
1. Create captivating email hero images to grab audience’s attention and push to call to action;
2. Design over 50 emails for multiple campaigns on Real Magnet;
3. Ensure email templates matched the campaign color palettes;
4. Enhance emails for easy digestion for audience – use of headers, stylizing and buttons.

• Assisted manager in settling business schedules through internal and external communication; also in recruiting, managing manufacture and export timeline & ensuring product quality;
• Made travel arrangements for Manager’s business trips;
• Translated contracts, advertisement and other documents as needed.

